 "card": "This PR upgrades the torcontrol fuzz target to route traffic through a mocked DynSock and construct valid Tor control values (such as v3 onion IDs and SAFECOOKIE HMACs) with replies up to 256 bytes. Previously, the fuzzer called TorController callbacks directly with short strings, missing wire buffer parsing and almost all success paths. The PR also fixes an existing bug in DynSock::Wait() that destroyed the socket instance on call return. Author measurements show line coverage of torcontrol.cpp increasing from 52.2% to 81.8% and branch coverage from 47.5% to 74.0%.",
